.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-collection-plan 1  "tapectl-collection-plan " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-collection\-plan \- Show the batch plan (alphabetical first\-fit, §7) for every configured collection\*(Aqs pending units
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl collection plan\fR [\fB\-\-copies\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-media\fR] [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the batch plan (alphabetical first\-fit, §7) for every configured collection\*(Aqs pending units
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-copies\fR \fI<COPIES>\fR [default: 2]
Copies to plan for — informational only (batches don\*(Aqt change; this scales the printed cartridge\-count estimate)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-\-media\fR \fI<MEDIA>\fR
Plan against this media generation rather than the drive\*(Aqs own (ADR\-0010) — e.g. sizing batches for LTO\-5 stock that an LTO\-6 drive will write. No cartridge need be loaded
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Which configured drive to plan against, by its device path. Only needed when more than one `[[backends.lto]]` is configured — without it, planning errored outright on a multi\-drive config rather than asking
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept (issue #147)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
